---
import { withBase } from "~/lib/site";
---

<section class="section-pad">
  <div class="container-wide grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-12">
    <header class="md:col-span-5 md:col-start-1 reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">The cottage story</p>
      <h2 class="mt-6 font-display display-xl">
        Where you finally <em>stop</em> answering email.
      </h2>
    </header>

    <div class="md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7 reveal" style="transition-delay: 160ms;">
      <p class="body-prose drop-cap">
        The first time most guests come to Captain's Cottage, they arrive on a Friday evening, half-frantic from the drive down, and step onto the screened porch to a kind of quiet they had forgotten about. The dock catches the last of the sun. An osprey works the creek. Inside the cottage, three bedrooms, a wood-burning kitchen, the cedar sauna warming for whoever wants it first.
      </p>
      <p class="body-prose mt-6">
        By Sunday morning, no one is checking the time. Tide is the only schedule. The kids are pulling crab pots off the dock. The coffee is on the porch table. The book you brought is open to the same page you started on Friday because you keep getting up to look at the water.
      </p>
      <p class="body-prose mt-6">
        This is what the Northern Neck does. It is Virginia's quietest secret, a long peninsula reaching east where the Potomac meets the Chesapeake Bay. We bought the cottage nearly a decade ago and have been refining it ever since — every choice in service of the same idea: a place to disconnect, on the water, that does not feel like anything other than itself.
      </p>
      <a href={withBase("/the-cottage")} class="btn btn-ghost mt-10">
        Tour the cottage →
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
